@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Use case: product-mockup. Asset type: high-quality transparent front-view controller illustration embedded in an actual Windows emulator controls page. Create ONLY one isolated controller, large and sharply detailed, straight orthographic front/top view as seen looking down at the face of a controller resting flat. All controls visible. Realistic polished product-render quality with subtle matte material and precise engineering, no cartoon outline, no neon contour, no stand, no environment, no text labels outside the controller, no cables, no extra accessories. Keep the complete controller inside the image, even narrow transparent padding, true alpha transparent background and no ground plane/shadow outside the object. Landscape 3:2 composition, controller occupies most of width. Sharp edges at high DPI. Buttons must be anatomically located correctly. Subject: a recognizable white-and-black PlayStation DualSense controller with accurately sculpted white outer grips and distinctive black central face panel. Symmetrical left and right analog sticks aligned low near center, directional pad on upper-left, large rectangular touchpad in upper-center. Correct face-button diamond on upper-right: triangle at top, circle at right, cross at bottom, square at left. Subtle familiar muted colored glyphs or gray glyphs on clear buttons, precise clean symbols. Small Create and Options buttons flanking the touchpad. White shoulder L1/R1 at top and triggers behind. Small center home button and mute button. Correct broad DualSense shape, realistic subtle material shading, crisp high-quality render. No Xbox shape, no asymmetrical sticks, no extra buttons.
